  "reply": {
    "analysis_type": "paradigm_network",
    "rationale": "A limited paradigm network is defensible only for code families with clear substitution in a shared frame and predictable meanings: H+quality, P+pattern-state, verdict/status + optional followup marker, and several short region/state codes (C+/C-, Eo/E-/E~, Fo/F+/F-/Ff, T+/T-). The suggested family based on the shared string 'F-' from F-ok and F-rim- is rejected because the residues do not form a coherent compositional paradigm. Longer forms such as C-dark, E-fade, F-ok, F-rim-, H-thin, Hth, Hol, Dc, Flk, Cl, Bd, L, N are left lexical because no supported multi-entry segmentation is available. Standalone symbols like K and T remain lexical even when the same surface substring appears as a morpheme inside a structured entry; standalone entries with fewer than two morphemes cannot be paradigm entries.",
